@*
    THE common Task / Sub Task creation form.

    One dialog, included by every screen that can create task work, driven
    by wwwroot/js/Shared/task-form.js. Before this existed there were three
    implementations:

      1. Task Center "New Task (Custom)" -- a proper dialog (this layout)
      2. Task Center row menu "Add child task" -- FOUR chained
         window.prompt() / confirm() boxes
      3. Risk Treatment "Add a sub task" -- an inline panel with its own
         fields and its own validation

    Three forms, three validation rules, three sets of field names for one
    concept. This partial is the single one, and the JS decides what it is
    creating from the options it is opened with.

    FIELD SET -- unchanged from the reference
    ----------------------------------------
    Organization - Task Name* - Description - Assigned To* - Priority -
    Start Date - Target Date - Remarks, plus Parent Task and Mandatory in
    sub task mode. Nothing was removed to make it fit.

    FITTING IN ONE SCREEN
    ---------------------
    Sub task mode is the tall one: ten controls plus a header and an
    action row. Stacked one per line at 640px wide that is well past a
    768px-tall laptop viewport, so the dialog scrolled.

    Three changes, in order of how much height each returns:

      1. TWO COLUMNS THROUGHOUT, at 880px instead of 640px. The pairs the
         requirement names -- Assigned To / Priority, Start Date / Target
         Date -- were already side by side; Organization / Parent Task and
         Description / Remarks now are too. Four stacked rows become two.

      2. TIGHTER RHYTHM. Gaps 12px -> 10px, label margins 4px -> 3px,
         dialog padding 20/24 -> 16/20, header and action margins trimmed.
         Control padding and font size are UNCHANGED -- the requirement
         asks for less space between fields, not smaller fields.

      3. A STICKY ACTION ROW. Below ~600px of viewport the fields scroll
         inside the form while Cancel and Create stay put, so the buttons
         are reachable at any height rather than only when everything fits.

    Description and Remarks share a row rather than Remarks keeping its
    place at the end. Both are optional free text of the same kind, and
    pairing them is the single biggest height saving available without
    touching a field.

    Included ONCE per page. The ids are global, which is exactly what lets
    any screen on that page open the same dialog.
*@
<dialog id="gracTaskFormDialog" class="gtf">
    <form id="gracTaskForm" method="dialog" class="gtf-form">
        <header class="gtf-head">
            <h2 id="gracTaskFormTitle">New Task (Custom)</h2>
            <button type="button" id="gracTaskFormClose" class="gtf-x" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
        </header>

        <div id="gracTaskFormMessage" class="gtf-msg"></div>

        <div class="gtf-body">
            <div class="gtf-grid">
                @* Organization is context, not a choice: every caller
                   already knows which organisation it is working in, and
                   a picker here would let a task be created against one
                   the rest of the screen is not showing.

                   Spans both columns for a task; shares the row with
                   Parent Task for a sub task (see .is-subtask below). *@
                <div class="gtf-field gtf-org">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Organization</span>
                    <div class="gtf-org-box" id="gracTaskFormOrgLabel">&mdash;</div>
                </div>

                @* ---- Parent task (sub task mode only) ----------------
                   Two mutually exclusive cells, one shown at a time by
                   the JS:

                     ParentFixed  opened from a task's own menu, so the
                                  parent is known -- read-only, never
                                  editable
                     ParentPick   opened without a parent in hand, so the
                                  user chooses one

                   The fixed one is a disabled input rather than plain
                   text so it reads as a field the user cannot change,
                   which is what read-only should look like in a form. *@
                <label class="gtf-field gtf-parent" id="gracTaskFormParentFixed">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Parent Task</span>
                    <input type="text" id="gracTaskFormParentLabel" disabled />
                    <input type="hidden" id="gracTaskFormParentId" />
                    <span class="gtf-note">Set from the task you opened this from; it cannot be changed here.</span>
                </label>

                <label class="gtf-field gtf-parent" id="gracTaskFormParentPick">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Parent Task<i class="gtf-req">*</i></span>
                    <select id="gracTaskFormParentSelect">
                        <option value="">&mdash; select the parent task &mdash;</option>
                    </select>
                </label>

                <label class="gtf-field gtf-span2">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Task Name<i class="gtf-req">*</i></span>
                    <input type="text" id="gracTaskFormTitleInput" maxlength="250" required />
                </label>

                <label class="gtf-field">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Description</span>
                    <textarea id="gracTaskFormDescription" rows="4" maxlength="4000"></textarea>
                </label>

                <label class="gtf-field">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Remarks</span>
                    <textarea id="gracTaskFormRemarks" rows="4" maxlength="4000"></textarea>
                </label>

                <label class="gtf-field">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Assigned To<i class="gtf-req">*</i></span>
                    <select id="gracTaskFormAssignee" required>
                        <option value="">&mdash; select an employee &mdash;</option>
                    </select>
                </label>

                <label class="gtf-field">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Priority</span>
                    <select id="gracTaskFormPriority">
                        <option value="Low">Low</option>
                        <option value="Medium" selected>Medium</option>
                        <option value="High">High</option>
                        <option value="Critical">Critical</option>
                    </select>
                    <span class="gtf-note" id="gracTaskFormPriorityNote"></span>
                </label>

                <label class="gtf-field">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Start Date</span>
                    <input type="date" id="gracTaskFormStartDate" />
                    <span class="gtf-note" id="gracTaskFormStartNote"></span>
                </label>

                <label class="gtf-field">
                    <span class="gtf-label">Target Date</span>
                    <input type="date" id="gracTaskFormTargetDate" />
                </label>

                @* Sub task only. BRD §12: a mandatory child blocks its
                   parent's completion, which is the gate Risk Centre's
                   residual analysis depends on -- a real decision, not a
                   detail. *@
                <div class="gtf-check gtf-span2" id="gracTaskFormMandatoryRow">
                    <input type="checkbox" id="gracTaskFormMandatory" checked />
                    <label for="gracTaskFormMandatory">
                        Mandatory &mdash; the parent task cannot be completed while this sub task is open.
                    </label>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        @* Sticky, so Cancel and Create stay reachable even on a viewport
           short enough that the fields above have to scroll. *@
        <footer class="gtf-actions">
            <button type="button" id="gracTaskFormCancel" class="pm-button">Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" id="gracTaskFormSubmit" class="pm-button primary">Create Task</button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>

<style>
    /* Scoped to .gtf so nothing here can reach another dialog. */
    .gtf {
        border: none;
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 0;
        width: 94%;
        max-width: 880px;          /* was 640 -- two real columns need it */
        max-height: 92vh;          /* never taller than the viewport      */
        box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, .25);
        color: #0f172a;
    }
    .gtf::backdrop { background: rgba(15, 23, 42, .45); }

    /* The form is the flex column: head and actions hold their size, the
       body is the only part allowed to scroll -- and only when the
       viewport is genuinely too short. */
    .gtf-form {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        max-height: 92vh;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 16px 20px;
        gap: 10px;
    }
    .gtf-body { overflow-y: auto; min-height: 0; }

    .gtf-head {
        display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 12px; flex: 0 0 auto;
    }
    .gtf-head h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; }
    .gtf-x {
        background: none; border: 0; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1;
        cursor: pointer; color: #64748b; padding: 0 2px;
    }
    .gtf-x:hover { color: #dc2626; }

    .gtf-msg {
        display: none; flex: 0 0 auto;
        padding: 7px 11px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 13px;
    }

    /* Two columns. Every field is a grid cell; the ones that need the
       whole row say so. */
    .gtf-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 10px 14px;
        align-items: start;
    }
    .gtf-span2 { grid-column: span 2; }

    /* Organization owns the row on a task, and shares it with Parent Task
       on a sub task -- so neither mode leaves half a row empty. */
    .gtf-org { grid-column: span 2; }
    .gtf-form.is-subtask .gtf-org { grid-column: span 1; }

    /* Both parent cells are hidden until the JS shows the right one. */
    .gtf-parent { display: none; }

    .gtf-field { display: block; min-width: 0; }
    .gtf-label {
        display: block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
        color: #475569; margin-bottom: 3px;
    }
    .gtf-req { color: #dc2626; font-style: normal; margin-left: 2px; }

    /* Hidden by default: the Priority and Start Date notes only apply in
       sub task mode, and the JS shows them there. */
    .gtf-note {
        display: none; font-size: 11px; color: #64748b; margin-top: 3px;
    }

    /* The read-only parent's note is the exception -- that row is only
       ever visible when the note is true, so it needs no JS. */
    #gracTaskFormParentFixed .gtf-note { display: block; }

    /* Control size is deliberately NOT reduced: the requirement asks for
       less space between fields, not smaller fields. */
    .gtf-field input[type="text"],
    .gtf-field input[type="date"],
    .gtf-field select,
    .gtf-field textarea {
        width: 100%;
        padding: 6px 8px;
        border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font: inherit;
        font-size: 13px;
        color: #0f172a;
        background: #fff;
    }
    .gtf-field textarea { resize: vertical; min-height: 84px; }
    .gtf-field input:disabled,
    .gtf-field select:disabled,
    .gtf-field textarea:disabled { background: #f1f5f9; color: #334155; }

    .gtf-org-box {
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 5px; background: #f8fafc;
        padding: 6px 10px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 13px;
        overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .gtf-check { display: none; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; }
    .gtf-check label { font-size: 12px; color: #475569; line-height: 1.35; }
    .gtf-check input { margin-top: 2px; }

    .gtf-actions {
        display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 10px;
        flex: 0 0 auto; padding-top: 10px;
        border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    }

    /* One column on a narrow window. Below this the two-column pairs stop
       helping and start cramping. */
    @@media (max-width: 720px) {
        .gtf-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
        .gtf-span2, .gtf-org, .gtf-form.is-subtask .gtf-org { grid-column: span 1; }
    }

    /* On a short viewport the textareas give up height first -- they are
       the only controls with room to spare, and shrinking them keeps the
       fields on one screen without touching any single-line control. */
    @@media (max-height: 780px) {
        .gtf-field textarea { min-height: 62px; }
        .gtf-form { gap: 8px; }
        .gtf-grid { gap: 8px 14px; }
    }
</style>
